      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">6. Top 4 Audit Window Failure Traps & Remediation Runbook</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-slate-300">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">1. Silent API Token Disconnect During the Window:</strong> An OAuth token or AWS IAM role secret expires, causing Drata/Vanta to stop collecting logs for 30 consecutive days. <em>Mitigation:</em> Configure daily email/Slack notifications for integration health failures; assign integration maintenance to a primary DevOps lead.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">2. Offboarding Delays Exceeding 24-Hour Policy:</strong> Company policy states access is revoked within 24 hours of employee departure, but an HR offboarding ticket is closed 5 days late. <em>Mitigation:</em> Integrate your HRIS (Rippling, Gusto) directly with Okta/Google Workspace to automate instantaneous account deprovisioning.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">3. Annual Penetration Test Date Slippage:</strong> Waiting until Month 11 of a 12-month window to schedule an annual third-party pen test, risking audit conclusion before the report is finalized. <em>Mitigation:</em> Book your annual pen test 90 days before your audit window renewal deadline.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-white">4. GitHub Pull Requests Merged Without Peer Review:</strong> Administrators bypassing branch protection to push emergency patches directly to <code>main</code> without approval. <em>Mitigation:</em> Enforce branch protection rules with "Do not allow bypassing the above settings" enabled for repository admins.
          </li>
        </ul>
